.TH AV 1 2026-10-30 "av" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
av \- the Asciiverse client: browse, install and play terminal games
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B av
.br
.B av
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B av
is the Asciiverse client: the whole catalog of text-mode games, programs,
text adventures, art and MUDs in your terminal.
Run alone, it opens the catalog and your library: one list on the left, and
for the highlighted title its preview, store page and news on the right.
From there titles are installed, updated, uninstalled and started.
.PP
Every download is checked against the sha256 in the catalog before it is
unpacked.
Updates are only ever started by you.
.PP
With a command,
.B av
does that one thing and exits.
A
.I title
is its id, as in
.BR "av install solitty" ,
or its full name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI install " title" \fR...
Install titles, or update them to the catalog's version.
.TP
.BR update " [\fItitle\fR...]"
Update these titles, or every title with an update.
.TP
.BI uninstall " title" \fR...
Remove titles. Their saves and settings are kept.
.TP
.BI play " title" " \fR[\fIargs\fR]"
Start a title; extra arguments go after the catalog's own.
For a MUD, connect to it.
.TP
.BR list " [" installed | updates | wishlist ]
List the catalog, or part of it.
.TP
.BI search " words"
Find titles by name, topic, genre or developer.
.TP
.BI info " title"
Show a title's details and its newest news.
.TP
.BI completions " shell"
Print tab completion for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.B fish
or
.BR powershell .
The Debian package already installs it for bash, zsh and fish.
.TP
.B help
Show the commands.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show av's version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B \(ua \(da
Move in the list; \(ua at its top opens the card that chooses what the
list shows.
.TP
.BR / " or typing"
Search names, topics, genres and developers.
.TP
.B Enter
The title's actions: install, play, wishlist.
.TP
.B Tab
Move between the list, the actions and the page.
.TP
.B Space
In the show card, switch a box; on the page, pause the preview.
.TP
.B F1
Help.
.TP
.B F2
Downloads: progress, the queue, retry, and updates waiting.
.TP
.B F5
Fetch the catalog again.
.TP
.B Esc
Back one step; at the top, quit.
.PP
Dragging over a title's page copies its text.
Shift and drag selects anything on the screen, the terminal's own way.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AV_CATALOG_URL
Read the catalog from this address instead of Asciiverse's own.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log what av does to
.IR ~/.cache/asciiverse/av.log ,
for example
.BR RUST_LOG=av=debug .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
The commands print without colors.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/asciiverse/
Installed titles, in
.IR games/ ,
.I programs/
and
.IR movies/ ,
and the library:
.I installed.json
and
.IR wishlist.json .
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/
Each installed title is linked here by its id, so it also starts by name.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/asciiverse/
The catalog, downloads, previews and
.IR av.log ;
safe to delete.
.TP
.I ~/.config/asciiverse/
av's own settings, such as what the list shows.
.PP
These follow
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ,
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
and
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when they are set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when a command fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://asciiverse.sh
.UE
